    "Greek_timing": "ASR generates text/language without native word timestamps. Greek forced alignment is unsupported. Any later coarse input-window intervals must be explicitly labeled processing intervals, with an independently reviewed sample-covering chunk policy; neither token count nor generation time creates valid speech timestamps.",
    "product_implication": "A good text screen alone would not satisfy subtitle/word-timing, speaker-boundary or full-film completeness gates.",
    "raw_capture": "Retain full PCM/sample counts, input features/masks, raw generated IDs/EOS and untouched raw strings before parsing. The original qwen-asr parser repairs long repeats; native parser differs, so parsed text alone is insufficient provenance."
